# There are no pre-commit hooks: format a change before moving on from it.
# Formatters (taplo, rumdl, biome) and their scope: tools/jujutsu/fix.toml,
# which only `just fix` loads; a plain `jj fix` has no formatters. They come
# from mise, so run these where mise is active, or prefix `mise exec --`.

# Format the working-copy change, and any changes on top of it
just fix

# The habit: format, then start the next change
just fix && jj new -m "next thing"

# Format another change, and its descendants
just fix -s <change>

# Also format files the change didn't touch (the whole tree at that change)
just fix --include-unchanged-files

# Nothing is formatted below the starting change: revsets.fix is @ in
# fix.toml. Never widen -s to old history; that reformats commits written
# before these formatters existed.

# No dry run: fix, look, and take it back if you don't want it
just fix && jj diff
jj undo
